    "en": "Ducks: the males"
  },
  "subtitle": {
    "en": "Five ducks, each with one striking feature"
  },
  "intro": {
    "en": "Today it's the ducks' turn. In winter, drakes wear their smartest plumage, and they are easy to tell apart. The females look much more alike, and we leave those to a later course. Look for the males.\n\nEach of these five has one thing that gives it away: a hanging crest, a green eye stripe, a yellow forehead, a black rear end, a huge spoon-shaped bill. If you have the habit of looking at the shape first, as in week 4, you will get these quickly.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of eight questions, with birds from the last two weeks mixed in."
  },
  "words": [
